          "filename": "Rutland Railway Museum - geograph.org.uk - 1465702.jpg",
          "caption": "Rutland Railway Museum. The museum, on the site of Cottesmore Sidings (the end of a freight-only branch from Ashwell on the Melton-Oakham main line) is home to a fine collection of standard-gauge engines which worked \"on the ironstone\" in the East Midlands. The green corrugated-iron shed on the right was once Woolsthorpe Quarries' Harston Engine Shed. It was brought from its original location in NE Leicestershire 1461411 and rebuilt here.",
          "alt": "Rutland Railway Museum. The museum, on the site of Cottesmore Sidings (the end of a freight-only branch from Ashwell on the Melton-Oakham main line) is home to a fine collection of standard-gauge engines which worked \"on the ironstone\" in the East Midlands. The green corrugated-iron shed on the right was once Woolsthorpe Quarries' Harston Engine Shed. It was brought from its original location in NE Leicestershire 1461411 and rebuilt here.",
